  "notes": "Measured on 9H-MATI (Dash 8-400, left side, Gatwick, 2024-08-28) fitted to the Dash 8-400 shape; the blue aircraft were checked against it (9H-EVA 2023, 9H-PET and 9H-ALE 2024) and carry the same layout. The title runs x 0.19-0.44, baseline under the windows (y -0.25), ascenders to y 0.66 (about 2.5 m), lower case 0.63 of that, slanted. The tail's colour starts on the fuselage on a slanted line from the belly at x 0.825 to the crown at x 0.88, behind the aft door, and covers the tail cone. 'skyalps.com' on the nacelle is placed against the nacelle's ends in the photo (the nearer nacelle is out of the fuselage's plane), low confidence. SkyAlps flies its Dash 8s on its own Maltese certificate under ICAO SWU (9H-MATI flew as SWU1919 when the maintainer saw it); its fins are blue (standard) or a green forest (green), aircraft by aircraft. The fin's fields come straight off the photo (photo_trace fields, 0.5 m and up), the logo's disc hidden, so they're rough: what reads right is pale above and forward, trees in green through the middle and toward the trailing edge, dark at the foot. Worn by 9H-MATI and 9H-SOP (airframes/SWU.json). The long dorsal fairing ahead of the fin's leading edge is white (a white fin area left of its leading edge: the Dash 8 shape draws the dorsal in the fin's base colour otherwise).",
  "history": "New 2026-11-21 (the maintainer's sightings: 9H-MATI, callsign SWU1919)."
}
